<title>SPAIN: Bankinter says 97 earnings forecast conservative.</title>
<headline>Bankinter says 97 earnings forecast conservative.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1997-01-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Juan Arena, managing director of Bankinter, said on Tuesday the bank's 1997 forecast of earnings growth of 10 percent was conservative.</p>
<p>&quot;We are being conservative,&quot; Arena told Reuters Financial Television.</p>
<p>Earlier, Bankinter reported 1996 net earnings of 17.14 billion pesetas, up 12.1 percent over the prior year.</p>
<p>--Madrid Newsroom +34 1 585 2167</p>
